Z||000000||JohnnyK||05-13-2000||03:56 PM||||Just bought my new caliper, and as I was ready to install it, i took the wood out that was holding the piston back.. Well, it flew forware, crushed my finger, and left the bore.. I couldn't put it back in, but finally c-clamped it hard enough that it went right back in with a little click/bang noise..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Anyways.. This is a new caliper (rebuilt, same thing), and since there hasn';t been any fluid in it, wondering if this would wreck the seals.. I'm assuming not, since when you overhaul them anyways, you have to slide it that far out anyways and then in again (think that made sense).. This happened about 2-3 times.. Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||05-13-2000||04:30 PM||||Uh? I've never had that happen to me! Crushed your finger? I smell lawsuit...LOL! I wouldn't use that caliper after you "forced" it back in. Take back and get another one.||||reg||1
